bit prefix, the same fact the reserve count shows. `TestALockedOutSprayNeverReachesTheReserve` sprays 2^20 codes at a locked screen (with the KDF swapped for a hash so it runs in seconds) and the owner still claims on the next boot; `TestProductionKDF` pins the production cost. Residual: each post while the reserve has tries costs the box one 64 MiB derivation, serialized, so a flood of posts slows every answer, the owner's included, but takes no try from the owner. A state sealed before the reserve has no prefix and no reserve. | HW-10 acceptance 3 | A per-boot reserve larger than 3, a different prefix length or a different cost changes the residual figures; any short prefix tag brings back the online burner. |
